{"repositoryId":602765651,"availability":"available","full":"mattlol85/Fitz-Net","name":"Fitz-Net","description":"A collection of software that runs the Fitz-Net","category":"Other","language":"PowerShell","stars":2,"forks":1,"created":"2023-02-16T22:28:56Z","updated":"2026-10-18T03:03:31Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://fitznet.org/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T07:21:00.115Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T07:21:00.115Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T07:21:00.115Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-13T07:37:16.589Z","stars":2,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-19T07:21:00.115Z","stars":2,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["[][contributors-url] [][forks-url] [][stars-url] [][issues-url] [][license-url] [][linkedin-url]","Fitz-Net is a self-hosted, full-stack personal platform running on a home server — exposed to the internet via dynamic DNS. It's a place to build and ship real ideas, backed by real infrastructure: a Proxmox hypervisor, Docker containers, a Caddy reverse proxy, physical ESP32 hardware that talks to the backend over WebSockets, a self-hosted email server for fitznet.org, a Discord bot (Fitz-Bot) that manages a Minecraft server, and a full observability stack (Grafana, Loki, Prometheus, Promtail, cAdvisor)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mattlol85/Fitz-Net/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fbd90635ad117d7eceefb2ffa616b1c30fd96847d319c4fb7d062965dbe3e300","extractedAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:16.761Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:37:16.761Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"[][contributors-url] [][forks-url] [][stars-url] [][issues-url] [][license-url] [][linkedin-url]","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mattlol85/Fitz-Net/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"User management (register, login, JWT auth, profile update)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com